; A reference to a name its own declaration marks deprecated.
;
; The tag needed no compiler change to EXIST - the AXTAG key namespace
; is open, so `;@axiom:deprecated(...)` already parsed, was recorded,
; and was re-emitted on the AXSYM line as `#deprecated=`. What was
; missing was anything reading it. `scripts/check-compat.sh` reads it
; at one end (a removal whose baseline row carried the notice is
; RETIRED, not REMOVED) and this warning is the other end, the one a
; caller sees.
;
; A WARNING by design, not as a staging step: the release that
; ANNOUNCES a removal is the one release in which callers must still
; build. `tests/diagnostics/severity.policy` records that reasoning.
;@axiom:deprecated(use vecLen instead)
(pub :: oldLen (-> Int Int))

(pub fn (oldLen v) 0)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (oldLen 7))
